igned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535176 true] [17592186335566 1113 #uuid "17df8f70-560c-50cc-995c-b38203b5ea8b" 13194139535176 true] [17592186335566 1145 "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are elementary matrices." 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335568 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335569 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335570 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335571 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1000 #edb/ref 17592186335572 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1041 "selection" 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1104 #edb/ref 17592186335570 13194139535176 true] [17592186335567 1110 #uuid "7ddb4f9c-b793-51c0-9fde-49a175491b33" 13194139535176 true] [17592186335568 1034 "$A$ only" 13194139535176 true] [17592186335568 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 